{
  "slug": "mlflow",
  "name": "Mlflow",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Skills for tracing, evaluating, and improving AI agents with MLflow. Supports the full agent improvement loop: instrument → trace → evaluate → iterate → validate.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **12 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (12): `mlflow-agent` (Master dispatcher for all MLflow workflows), `agent-evaluation` (Use this when you need to EVALUATE OR IMPROVE or OPTIMIZE an existing LLM agent's output quality -…), `build-a-scorer` (Help the user go from zero to a shipped MLflow evaluation prototype by understanding their app, generalizing a…), `instrumenting-with-mlflow-tracing` (Instruments Python and TypeScript code with MLflow Tracing for observability), `analyze-mlflow-trace` (Analyzes a single MLflow trace to answer a user query about it), `analyze-mlflow-chat-session` (Analyzes an MLflow session — a sequence of traces from a multi-turn chat conversation or interaction), `retrieving-mlflow-traces` (Retrieves MLflow traces using CLI or Python API), `querying-mlflow-metrics` (Fetches aggregated trace metrics (token usage, latency, trace counts, quality evaluations) from MLflow tracking servers), and 4 more\n- **Hooks** (1): `UserPromptSubmit`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install mlflow@claude-plugins-official` from `mlflow/skills`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 12,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "MLflow Team"
  },
